  "title": "Santos-Dumont 14-bis flights at Bagatelle",
  "summary": "In autumn 1906 Alberto Santos-Dumont flew his 14-bis aircraft in Paris. A flight on 23 October of nearly 60 metres was certified by the Aéro Club de France, and on 12 November at Bagatelle he covered 220 metres in about 21 seconds, described as the first world aviation record.",
